```

In this solution, we use dynamic programming to solve the problem efficiently. The `dp` array stores the length of the longest repeating subsequence ending at each position. We iterate through the string and update the `dp` array based on whether the current character matches or not. Finally, we return the maximum value from the last element of the `dp` array, which represents the length of the longest repeating subsequence.

